{
  "_source": "Hand-worked in evaluate-template-v2 (E1 and E2, summary and month-by-month sheets), redone from evaluate-template.xlsx (v1) for seat 2's answers on #34 (D28-D30 v2). Not derived from engine code. D1 grant rework (seat 2 on #49) in the V3 REWORK block of evaluate-template-v2-d1.xlsx (a copy of evaluate-template-v2): the D12 refund redone without the GRANT rows (own-CPF refund), the grant part, and net position with it added back.",
  "_workedBy": "seat 1",
  "_dateWorked": "2026-10-11",
  "_checkedBy": "Independent script recomputation from the written rules of every summary figure and yearly row (106 figures, matches to the cent); figures transcribed from the sheet by script; D1 grant rework: own-CPF refund, grant part and net position for E1 and E2 recomputed independently from the D12 rules (6 figures, match to the cent), transcribed by script",
  "_conventions": {
    "decisions": "Contract v2.1 notes plus D28-D32 as updated on #34 (v2)",
    "prices": "choice.purchasePriceCents and choice.marketValueAtKeysCents are TODAY's values (evaluationStartYear); evaluate() grows them month-precisely (D31): value x (1 + g)^(months / 12), rounded to the cent at each step (BTO market value is rounded at keys, then grown to the horizon)",
    "horizon": "Growth and CPF are measured to 1 Jan of horizonYear + 1",
    "netPosition": "D1 with grants (seat 2 on #49): market value - loan - CPF refund (principal + accrued interest) + cpfGrantRefundCents - clawback - housing cash. cpfGrantRefundCents = the full refund less the refund redone by D12 without the GRANT rows; a difference, so the parts sum to the cent. The refund fields and yearly cpfObligationEndCents still show the full refund",
    "funding": "D28 v2: grants, then OA above the retention, then the loan, then cash. Retention: each buyer keeps up to loans.hdbLoanOaRetentionPerBuyer of their own OA (stated assumption: the full amount, or their whole OA if less); the household keeps the sum. Stamp duty then legal fees from the OA left (whole fee or none), else cash; agent fees and renovation in cash. A grant left over after the price goes to the CPF Special/Retirement and MediSave accounts (HDB; seat 2 on #46), so it never reaches the OA and isn't refund principal",
    "btoStages": "D30 v2: signing = application + monthsToAgreementForLease (a stated assumption); at signing, loans.btoDownpaymentStages.hdbLoan.atSigningPercent of the price from grants first (D29 v2), then OA above the retention, then cash, plus stamp duty and legal fees; the rest at keys. Each grant part is a GRANT ledger entry dated when used",
    "cpfUsedCents": "Yearly cash flow counts OA savings withdrawn (lump sums, fees, instalments), EXCLUDING grants; grants are still CPF refund principal",
    "cashRequiredAtPurchaseCents": "Cash paid on the purchase date(s), excluding renovation and rent",
    "warnings": "Contract WARNINGS codes only; the OA running out is visible in yearlyCashFlow, not a warning. E2 warns LOAN_ABOVE_LIMIT: the loan needed ($308,600) is above the max loan ($300,000)"
  },
  "_units": "All money in integer cents.",
